[{"label": "malformed blank", "record": {"knowledge_point": {"db_id": 17592186059679, "id": "322168bb-52e3-5352-a2e3-c5bdbf2bc13e", "title": "Computing Higher Order Derivatives"}, "question": {":question/id": "cac6d676-2221-5259-af73-33906ac2056a", ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy", ":question/problem": "Given $g(x)=2{x}^{5}-3{x}^{3},$ we have\n\n${g}^{\u2034}(x)=$ \n{{field-1}}.", ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{5}-3{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =10{x}^{4}-9{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2033}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(10{x}^{4}-9{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =40{x}^{3}-18x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the third derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2034}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(40{x}^{3}-18x) \\\\  & =120{x}^{2}-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$", ":question/answer-fields": [{":answer-field/id": "4d5de520-92d2-5e44-9a19-b71ca1fcdb2c", ":answer-field/key": "field-1", ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank", ":answer-field/choices": [{":answer/id": "8c659d9c-65ec-57d1-81ed-446c0647cb66", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "6 (20 x^{2} - 3)"}], ":answer-field/correct": [":answer/id", "8c659d9c-65ec-57d1-81ed-446c0647cb66"]}]}, "generation": {"version": "higher-order-derivatives-2026-10-14-v1", "template": "polynomial", "profile": "blank", "seed": 0, "parameters": {"scales": [1, 1]}, "source_id": "q-343075", "source_basis": 2275, "source_lineage": "01a12a15-3e0a-75a1-9dac-f8b8c5d5c3f1", "order": 3, "domain": "real x", "recipes": ["correct"], "evidence_only": false, "eligible_for_learning": true, "mathematical_fingerprint": "cba85b8aa420d8d421c8ce952c9a748dafc0a28a0067ae75165f2ad64206c703", "dependencies": {"python": "3.13.5", "sympy": "1.14.0"}, "source_repairs": [], "math_format": "course-academy-tex-v1"}}, "checks": [{"submitted": "not mathematics", "expected": "unresolved", "purpose": "malformed diagnostic only"}]}, {"label": "foreign radio identity", "record": {"knowledge_point": {"db_id": 17592186059679, "id": "322168bb-52e3-5352-a2e3-c5bdbf2bc13e", "title": "Computing Higher Order Derivatives"}, "question": {":question/id": "4853ec42-a4eb-50c9-bc26-5d2884ee78d2", ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate", ":question/problem": "Given $h(x)=3{x}^{2}-5x+\\frac{3}{x},$ find ${h}^{\u2034}(x).$", ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that we can rewrite the function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(x) & =3{x}^{2}-5x+\\frac{3}{x} \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-5x+3{x}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2}-5x+3{x}^{-1}) \\\\  & =6x-5-3{x}^{-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{\u2033}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x-5-3{x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =6+6{x}^{-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the third derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{\u2034}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6+6{x}^{-3}) \\\\  & =-18{x}^{-4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{{x}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$", ":question/answer-fields": [{":answer-field/id": "f04ca1aa-147e-50a4-99cc-35742b6c7843", ":answer-field/key": "selection", ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio", ":answer-field/choices": [{":answer/id": "5de157b7-c5cd-5df8-80d2-3bd12b83d47a", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "6 (1 + \\frac{1}{x^{3}}) - \\frac{6}{x^{3}}"}, {":answer/id": "7c726c41-61ca-5d46-9afb-03c179530690", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "6 x - 5 - \\frac{3}{x^{2}}"}, {":answer/id": "418737b5-37e7-5f83-b042-2f92f5c5e70b", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "6 (1 + \\frac{1}{x^{3}})"}, {":answer/id": "837bf81e-6a04-5037-a8b2-8869badf9543", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "- \\frac{18}{